mn82:42.19 starts: Clad in a shroud, he leaves his wealth
mn82:42.20 starts: Prodded with stakes he burns upon the pyre.
mn82:42.21 starts: And as he dies, no relatives or friends
mn82:42.22 starts: Can offer him shelter and refuge here.
mn82:42.35 starts: Better is wisdom here than any wealth,
mn82:42.36 starts: Since by wisdom one gains the final goal.
mn82:42.37 starts: For people through ignorance do evil deeds
mn82:42.38 starts: While failing to reach the goal from life
sn1.18:1.1 starts: “Is there a person somewhere in the world
sn1.18:1.2 starts: Who is restrained by a sense of shame,
sn1.18:1.3 starts: One who draws back from blame
sn1.18:1.4 starts: As a good horse does from the whip?”
